 "styleRules": [
  "Shape first: chunky, rounded volumes at real-world scale (1 stud = 0.28 m; door 4 x 7.5, spruce 35-50, oak 25-30, logs 1 stud thick). Every edge carries a soft bevel or rounding (>= 0.1 stud); no razor edges, no thin slivers.",
  "Foliage is sculpted, closed clump volumes (SDF smooth-unions of boughs / leaf masses, meshed and decimated), never alpha cards: spruce = drooping fanned tiers, broadleaf = big lumpy masses with flatter undersides and gaps that show the limbs.",
  "Colour is painted, not photographed: every albedo is a soft value gradient (light tops / tips / outer crown -> dark undersides / interiors, warm-cool drift over 5-15 studs) multiplied by baked AO (near 0.6-1.8 + far 2.5-6 studs). No noise or grain finer than ~0.3 stud.",
  "Normal maps hold only soft, large detail (bark plates, leaf-mass lumps, wood grain, stone pitting) at moderate strength; silhouettes and big forms come from geometry.",
  "Palette: slightly desaturated naturals (sRGB) - needles 20-100, broadleaf green channel 38-145, bark 50-130, weathered logs 95-160, stone 90-160, soil 60-130; saturated accents only small and purposeful.",
  "Materials are matte PBR: roughness 0.74-0.95 for nature and wood, metalness 0 (no map); glass is the only smooth surface.",
  "Organic assets get one unique 1024 page each (Color+AO / Normal / Roughness 512, ~15-40 px/stud, shared by all parts of the asset). Buildings use a shared kit page: tiling trims (logs, planks, shakes, end grain) at 50-128 px/stud with contact occlusion painted in, plus a uniquely baked region for stonework.",
  "Terrain MaterialVariants are 1024 px tiles over 10-12 studs (85-100 px/stud) built from modelled elements (rounded pebbles, leaves, twigs) rendered top-down in Blender: clean shapes, soft contact AO, broad colour drift only, MaterialPattern Organic.",
  "Budgets: trees <= 15k tris, buildings <= 16k, rocks <= 2k, every MeshPart < 20k; GLB with tangents, normals and UVs, single-sided, metallicFactor 0.",
  "Collision as gameplay reads: canopies and needles non-colliding (hide-able), trunks Hull, climbable oak wood PreciseConvexDecomposition + Climbable tag + Perch attachments, walls with openings PreciseConvexDecomposition."
 ],
 "import": [
  "Import StyleTest_C.glb (3D Importer / Open Cloud). Each asset root arrives as a Model of MeshParts named <Asset>_<Role>[_n]; re-centre with the asset 'origin' (WorldPivot = CFrame.new(origin), then PivotTo). The importer turns every import 180 degrees about Y (measured on all earlier sets) - undo it.",
  "Give every part ONE SurfaceAppearance from its surfaceAppearance block (ColorMap / NormalMap / RoughnessMap = uploaded ids of those PNGs, MetalnessMap empty, AlphaMode Overlay, Color white). All parts of one asset share the same three images, so copies instance. Normal maps are OpenGL (+Y) tangent space. Clear any importer TextureID; replace importer-made SurfaceAppearances (their roughness is half size).",
  "Per part: CanCollide = collide, CollisionFidelity = collision (edit time, via CreateMeshPartAsync), CastShadow, CanQuery, CanTouch, Anchored = true, Material = robloxMaterial (physics / footsteps), Color = rgb (fallback), Transparency = transparency (cabin glass 0.35).",
  "Attachments: StyleC_Oak Perch1-4 (level tops of standable limbs); StyleC_Cabin Door (threshold, facing out) and Hearth. Tag StyleC_Oak_Bark with CollectionService 'Climbable'.",
  "Terrain: make one MaterialVariant per terrainMaterials entry under MaterialService (ColorMap / NormalMap / RoughnessMap, StudsPerTile, MaterialPattern Organic, BaseMaterial as suggested) and apply it with MaterialService:SetBaseMaterialOverride or paint it into an Expanded Terrain slot."
 ],
